  "topic": "Read and write Sheen (ش) at the beginning, middle and end of words, with Fatha, Kasra and Damma.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "learn": [
    {
      "en": "This is Sheen. Like 'sh' in 'ship' or 'shine'. Tongue back, lips slightly forward a soft hushing sound.",
      "title": "Meet Sheen!",
      "ar": "ش",
      "aud": "c-0-ar",
      "tr": "Sheen"
    },
    {
      "en": "Same as Sin (three humps) but with THREE dots above. Three dots = Shin! ☀ Shin shines with THREE dots like a shining sun above three waves — Sh for Shine!",
      "title": "How to write Sheen"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a fatha, Sheen says “sha”.",
      "title": "Sheen with fatha",
      "ar": "شَ",
      "aud": "c-2-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a kasra, Sheen says “she”.",
      "title": "Sheen with kasra",
      "ar": "شِ",
      "aud": "c-3-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "With a damma, Sheen says “sho”.",
      "title": "Sheen with damma",
      "ar": "شُ",
      "aud": "c-4-ar"
    },
    {
      "en": "“The sun is shining”",
      "title": "Sentence of the lesson",
      "ar": "الشَّمْسُ مُشْرِقَة",
      "aud": "c-5-ar",
      "tr": "Al-Shamso Moshreqah"
    }
